# Ownership for the files that reach production without a human in the
# loop: a push to main touching functions/, firestore.rules or
# storage.rules auto-deploys.
#
# NOTE: do NOT enable "Require review from Code Owners" in branch
# protection while there is a single owner. GitHub does not let an author
# approve their own pull request, so a solo maintainer would be unable to
# merge anything — the rule would block the repo rather than protect it.
# This file is here so ownership is recorded, and so the setting becomes
# one click the day a second maintainer exists.

*                           @Cosaxo

# The privacy surface. Changes here are the ones worth a second read.
/firestore.rules            @Cosaxo
/storage.rules              @Cosaxo
/firestore-tests/           @Cosaxo
/functions/                 @Cosaxo

# Anything that reaches production, or decides what does.
/.github/workflows/         @Cosaxo
/docs/DECISIONS.md          @Cosaxo
